From 00233c4f56df34eb5158cde18abdd81ce481260e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 20:09:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 627/638] aros: --aros-native-threadpool wakes the idle worker
 on the least-loaded core

Which idle worker the thread group wakes IS the placement decision on
AROS: a task runs on whichever worker picks it up and a worker never
leaves its core, and exec's own placement (rom/exec/signal.c:190-199)
takes the first set bit rather than the least-loaded core. Chromium's
default - front of the idle set - is right on an OS that rebalances and
piles work onto one core here.

WorkerThread samples KrnGetCPUNumber() once in ThreadMain() (the only
thread that can answer for itself; stable because nothing migrates it).
TakeIdleWorkerOnLeastLoadedCoreLockRequired() counts awake workers per
core under lock_ and wakes the idle worker on the lightest one. Off by
default; the default Take() path is untouched.

Unmeasured so far: every earlier comparison ran with all workers on
CPU 0 (see the pin-workers commit), so this degenerated to "first idle
worker" and compared one policy against itself. The comment says so.


